course: dictionary
lesson: 3015
title: Dwindle: getting smaller bit by bit
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To dwindle means to become smaller, fewer or weaker little by little, until very little is left. Look at the clues around it. «The voice died away and ceased as an insect's tiny trumpet dwindles swiftly into silence» shows a sound getting quieter and quieter until there is nothing left.
explain: The Rat saw «but a distant speck on the white surface of the road». A speck gets smaller as it goes further away, so the speck is dwindling in size. Dwindle is a verb, which means it describes an action. Its adjective form is dwindling, as in «dwindling numbers».
explain: Money can dwindle too. «Dishonest money dwindles away, but whoever gathers money little by little makes it grow» (Proverbs 13:11). Here dwindle is the opposite of grow. To check your meaning, swap in "get smaller" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Dwindle means to become smaller, fewer or weaker little by little.
fact: «Dwindling» is the adjective form, and it means getting smaller.
fact: Phrases you may meet are «dwindling numbers», «dwindle away» and «dwindling supplies».
fact: «Dwindling numbers» of animals or forests show a problem, because there are fewer and fewer of them left.
fact: Dwindle is often the opposite of grow, so «dwindling supplies» means supplies that are running low.
exercise: «Supplies dwindled as the explorers walked on.» What does dwindled mean? | Stayed exactly the same | Turned into ice | Got bigger | *Became smaller little by little
exercise: Scientists worry about the dwindling numbers of bees. What does dwindling mean here? | Getting older | Getting warmer | Getting louder | *Getting smaller
exercise: Which word means the same as dwindle? | Sparkle | Grow | Shout | *Shrink
test: The candles dwindled until only a short stub was left. What happened to the candles? | Burned out in one second | *Got smaller bit by bit | Grew taller | Stayed exactly the same
test: Which sentence shows something getting weaker little by little? | The crowd cheered louder and louder | The bright sun burst through the clouds | The stream rushed and flooded the field | *The sound of the drum dwindled into silence
exam: Mia reads «dwindling supplies» in her story. What does it mean? | Supplies that are being carried up a hill | Supplies that are hidden in a box | Supplies that are brand new and never used | *Supplies that are getting smaller and running low
